{"kLim":{"title":"Limit","mc":"#15803d","body":"<div class=\"m-meta\"><p class=\"role\">The value <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> gets arbitrarily close to as <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span></span></span></span> gets close to <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span></span></span></span>.</p><div class=\"where\">📍 Location: <a data-go=\"T1\">App overview</a> › <a data-go=\"T2\">Agent</a> › <a data-go=\"T3\">LLM</a> › <a data-go=\"N\">Neural Network Basics</a> › <a data-go=\"K1\">Math · Calculus</a> › <b>Limit</b></div><span class=\"status no\">📐 Math foundation: not a component, but the rule behind the computation</span></div><div class=\"tryit\"><b>🧪 Try it: </b><button class=\"btn primary\" data-jump=\"labSecant\" data-lv=\"K1\">🧪 Secant to tangent (Calculus)</button></div><div class=\"m-tabs\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Card sections\"><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t0\" aria-controls=\"mt@p0\" aria-selected=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\">🎯 What it does</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t1\" aria-controls=\"mt@p1\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">▶ How to use</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t2\" aria-controls=\"mt@p2\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">🧠 Why</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t3\" aria-controls=\"mt@p3\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">⚠️ Limits</button></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p0\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t0\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"sec\"><h4>🎯 Role</h4><ul class=\"pts\"><li>Gives “arbitrarily close” a precise meaning; derivatives and integrals are built on it.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p1\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t1\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><div class=\"sec\" style=\"background:#f0f9ff\"><h4>▶ How to use it</h4><ul class=\"pts\"><li>A derivative is the limit of the secant slope as h → 0.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p2\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t2\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><div class=\"sec why\"><h4>🧠 Why it’s designed this way (the logic underneath)</h4><p>Looking only at the value is not enough: an expression like 0/0 has no value at that point, yet nearby values may settle towards a number.</p></div><div class=\"sec eff\"><h4>✅ Why this works</h4><p>The ε-δ definition turns “close” into inequalities that can be checked, so results can be proved rigorously.</p></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p3\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t3\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><p class=\"lim\">⚠️ Limits / notes: A limit may not exist (e.g. the two sides approach different numbers).</p></div><!--m2pi--><div class=\"sn\"><p class=\"sn-h\"><span>🔤 Symbols used here</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-all\" data-sym=\"*\">📖 All symbols</button></p><ul class=\"sn-l\"><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>f</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “f”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">a function: a “machine” that takes in a number and gives back a number</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"fx\">□( )</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “… of …”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">What comes out when you put the thing in brackets into the “machine” (function) named in front. Like a vending machine: put something in, get something out.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>x</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “x”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the input number</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>a</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “a”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the number x gets close to</span></li></ul></div><!--/m2pi-->"},"kDer":{"title":"Derivative","mc":"#15803d","body":"<div class=\"m-meta\"><p class=\"role\">The instantaneous rate of change: if the input moves a little, how many times as much the output moves.</p><div class=\"where\">📍 Location: <a data-go=\"T1\">App overview</a> › <a data-go=\"T2\">Agent</a> › <a data-go=\"T3\">LLM</a> › <a data-go=\"N\">Neural Network Basics</a> › <a data-go=\"K1\">Math · Calculus</a> › <b>Derivative</b></div><span class=\"status no\">📐 Math foundation: not a component, but the rule behind the computation</span></div><div class=\"tryit\"><b>🧪 Try it: </b><button class=\"btn primary\" data-jump=\"labSecant\" data-lv=\"K1\">🧪 Secant to tangent (Calculus)</button></div><div class=\"m-tabs\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Card sections\"><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t0\" aria-controls=\"mt@p0\" aria-selected=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\">🎯 What it does</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t1\" aria-controls=\"mt@p1\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">▶ How to use</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t2\" aria-controls=\"mt@p2\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">🧠 Why</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t3\" aria-controls=\"mt@p3\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">⚠️ Limits</button></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p0\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t0\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"sec\"><h4>🎯 Role</h4><ul class=\"pts\"><li>Definition: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>lim</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f&#x27;(x)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0019em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.355em;vertical-align:-0.345em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mop\">lim</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">h</span><span class=\"mrel mtight\">→</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.01em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">h</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.485em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mopen mtight\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">x</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">h</span><span class=\"mclose mtight\">)</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mopen mtight\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">x</span><span class=\"mclose mtight\">)</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.345em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span></span></span></span>.</li><li>Geometrically it is the slope of the tangent line.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p1\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t1\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><div class=\"sec\" style=\"background:#f0f9ff\"><h4>▶ How to use it</h4><ul class=\"pts\"><li>In training, look at the derivative of the loss with respect to a parameter: if positive, decrease the parameter; if negative, increase it.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p2\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t2\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><div class=\"sec why\"><h4>🧠 Why it’s designed this way (the logic underneath)</h4><p>The derivative gives the local linear approximation <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≈</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x+h)\\approx f(x)+f&#x27;(x)\\,h</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0019em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span></span></span></span>: within a small step a complicated function behaves like a line.</p></div><div class=\"sec eff\"><h4>✅ Why this works</h4><p>The error of this approximation shrinks faster than h (as h → 0), so small parameter steps reliably lower the loss.</p></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p3\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t3\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><p class=\"lim\">⚠️ Limits / notes: ReLU has no derivative at 0; frameworks use 0 there by convention (or another subgradient).</p></div><!--m2pi--><div class=\"sn\"><p class=\"sn-h\"><span>🔤 Symbols used here</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-all\" data-sym=\"*\">📖 All symbols</button></p><ul class=\"sn-l\"><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>f</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “f”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">a function: a “machine” that takes in a number and gives back a number</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"prime\">□′</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “prime”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">The little mark means “derivative”: how fast the function is changing at this point, like how steep a slope is.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"fx\">□( )</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “… of …”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">What comes out when you put the thing in brackets into the “machine” (function) named in front. Like a vending machine: put something in, get something out.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>x</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “x”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the input number</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"lim\">lim</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “limit”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">“When we get closer and closer, which number do we end up near?” The small text below says what is getting close to what.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>h</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “h”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">a small step: a tiny number that is not 0</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"to\">→</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “tends to”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">“Gets closer and closer to” the thing on the right, without having to reach it.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"frac\">▭⁄▭</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “over” (the fraction bar)</span><span class=\"sn-m\">The top is divided by the bottom. ½ is 1 divided by 2, which is one half.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"approx\">≈</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “is about”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">The two sides are nearly the same, but maybe not exactly: 3.14159… ≈ 3.14.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"mul\">□□</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: no word: side by side means times</span><span class=\"sn-m\">Two things written right next to each other, with no sign between them, are multiplied: a number right before a letter means that number times it; two brackets side by side are multiplied.</span></li></ul></div><!--/m2pi-->"},"kChain":{"title":"Chain rule","mc":"#15803d","body":"<div class=\"m-meta\"><p class=\"role\">The derivative of a composition is the product of the layers’ derivatives: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>g</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo mathvariant=\"normal\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><msup><mi>g</mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(f\\circ g)&#x27;(x)=f&#x27;(g(x))\\,g&#x27;(x)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">∘</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0019em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0019em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">))</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>.</p><div class=\"where\">📍 Location: <a data-go=\"T1\">App overview</a> › <a data-go=\"T2\">Agent</a> › <a data-go=\"T3\">LLM</a> › <a data-go=\"N\">Neural Network Basics</a> › <a data-go=\"K1\">Math · Calculus</a> › <b>Chain rule</b></div><span class=\"status no\">📐 Math foundation: not a component, but the rule behind the computation</span></div><div class=\"tryit\"><b>🧪 Try it: </b><button class=\"btn primary\" data-jump=\"labGradCheck\" data-lv=\"K5\">🧪 Backprop vs numerical gradient (Derivations)</button></div><div class=\"m-tabs\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Card sections\"><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t0\" aria-controls=\"mt@p0\" aria-selected=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\">🎯 What it does</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t1\" aria-controls=\"mt@p1\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">▶ How to use</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t2\" aria-controls=\"mt@p2\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">🧠 Why</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t3\" aria-controls=\"mt@p3\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">⚠️ Limits</button></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p0\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t0\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"sec\"><h4>🎯 Role</h4><ul class=\"pts\"><li>A neural network is a composition of layers; the chain rule splits the overall derivative into small per-layer ones.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p1\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t1\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><div class=\"sec\" style=\"background:#f0f9ff\"><h4>▶ How to use it</h4><ul class=\"pts\"><li>Backpropagation = start from the loss and multiply these small derivatives backwards through the computation graph.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p2\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t2\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><div class=\"sec why\"><h4>🧠 Why it’s designed this way (the logic underneath)</h4><p>Each layer only needs its own local derivative, not the shape of the whole network.</p></div><div class=\"sec eff\"><h4>✅ Why this works</h4><p>It is proved rigorously (see this stop), so multiplying layer by layer gives the exact gradient, not an approximation.</p></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p3\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t3\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><p class=\"lim\">⚠️ Limits / notes: Multiplying many layers’ derivatives can shrink the product (vanishing gradients) or blow it up (exploding gradients).</p></div><!--m2pi--><div class=\"sn\"><p class=\"sn-h\"><span>🔤 Symbols used here</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-all\" data-sym=\"*\">📖 All symbols</button></p><ul class=\"sn-l\"><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>f</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “f”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the second machine (applied next)</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"circ\">∘</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “composed with” (little circle)</span><span class=\"sn-m\">“Two machines joined up”: first the one on the right, then its result goes into the one on the left.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>g</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “g”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the first machine (applied first)</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"prime\">□′</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “prime”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">The little mark means “derivative”: how fast the function is changing at this point, like how steep a slope is.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"fx\">□( )</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “… of …”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">What comes out when you put the thing in brackets into the “machine” (function) named in front. Like a vending machine: put something in, get something out.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>x</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “x”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the input number</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"mul\">□□</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: no word: side by side means times</span><span class=\"sn-m\">Two things written right next to each other, with no sign between them, are multiplied: a number right before a letter means that number times it; two brackets side by side are multiplied.</span></li></ul></div><!--/m2pi-->"},"kGrad":{"title":"Partial derivatives & gradient","mc":"#15803d","body":"<div class=\"m-meta\"><p class=\"role\">With several inputs, differentiate with respect to each one (holding the rest fixed) and stack the results into a vector <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∇</mi><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\nabla f</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∇</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span></span></span></span>.</p><div class=\"where\">📍 Location: <a data-go=\"T1\">App overview</a> › <a data-go=\"T2\">Agent</a> › <a data-go=\"T3\">LLM</a> › <a data-go=\"N\">Neural Network Basics</a> › <a data-go=\"K1\">Math · Calculus</a> › <b>Partial derivatives &amp; gradient</b></div><span class=\"status no\">📐 Math foundation: not a component, but the rule behind the computation</span></div><div class=\"tryit\"><b>🧪 Try it: </b><button class=\"btn primary\" data-jump=\"labGD\" data-lv=\"K4\">🧪 Learning rate and convergence (Optimization)</button></div><div class=\"m-tabs\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Card sections\"><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t0\" aria-controls=\"mt@p0\" aria-selected=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\">🎯 What it does</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t1\" aria-controls=\"mt@p1\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">▶ How to use</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t2\" aria-controls=\"mt@p2\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">🧠 Why</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t3\" aria-controls=\"mt@p3\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">⚠️ Limits</button></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p0\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t0\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"sec\"><h4>🎯 Role</h4><ul class=\"pts\"><li>The gradient points in the direction of fastest increase; its length is the rate of change in that direction.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p1\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t1\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><div class=\"sec\" style=\"background:#f0f9ff\"><h4>▶ How to use it</h4><ul class=\"pts\"><li>Gradient descent takes a small step along −∇L; a large model has hundreds of billions of parameters, so the gradient has that many entries.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p2\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t2\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><div class=\"sec why\"><h4>🧠 Why it’s designed this way (the logic underneath)</h4><p>Trying one parameter at a time is far too slow; the gradient gives every direction at once.</p></div><div class=\"sec eff\"><h4>✅ Why this works</h4><p>The “fastest increase” claim is proved with the Cauchy–Schwarz inequality (see the Optimization stop).</p></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p3\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t3\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><p class=\"lim\">⚠️ Limits / notes: The gradient only describes a small neighbourhood; further away the function can look entirely different.</p></div><!--m2pi--><div class=\"sn\"><p class=\"sn-h\"><span>🔤 Symbols used here</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-all\" data-sym=\"*\">📖 All symbols</button></p><ul class=\"sn-l\"><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"nabla\">∇</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “nabla” or “del”: the gradient</span><span class=\"sn-m\">The “gradient”: how fast things change in each input direction, put in a list. It points the steepest way uphill; training takes a small step the opposite way so the loss goes down.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>f</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “f”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">a function: a “machine” that takes in a number and gives back a number</span></li></ul></div><!--/m2pi-->"},"kInt":{"title":"Integral","mc":"#15803d","body":"<div class=\"m-meta\"><p class=\"role\">The limit of adding up many tiny pieces; geometrically, the area under a curve.</p><div class=\"where\">📍 Location: <a data-go=\"T1\">App overview</a> › <a data-go=\"T2\">Agent</a> › <a data-go=\"T3\">LLM</a> › <a data-go=\"N\">Neural Network Basics</a> › <a data-go=\"K1\">Math · Calculus</a> › <b>Integral</b></div><span class=\"status no\">📐 Math foundation: not a component, but the rule behind the computation</span></div><div class=\"m-tabs\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Card sections\"><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t0\" aria-controls=\"mt@p0\" aria-selected=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\">🎯 What it does</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t1\" aria-controls=\"mt@p1\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">▶ How to use</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t2\" aria-controls=\"mt@p2\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">🧠 Why</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" id=\"mt@t3\" aria-controls=\"mt@p3\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">⚠️ Limits</button></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p0\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t0\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"sec\"><h4>🎯 Role</h4><ul class=\"pts\"><li>Probabilities and expectations of continuous random variables are integrals.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p1\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t1\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><div class=\"sec\" style=\"background:#f0f9ff\"><h4>▶ How to use it</h4><ul class=\"pts\"><li>The training objective “average loss over all data” is an expectation, written as an integral or a sum.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p2\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t2\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><div class=\"sec why\"><h4>🧠 Why it’s designed this way (the logic underneath)</h4><p>Fundamental theorem of calculus: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac{d}{dx}\\int_a^x f(t)\\,dt=f(x)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.2359em;vertical-align:-0.3558em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8801em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">d</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">x</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">d</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.345em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mop op-symbol small-op\" style=\"margin-right:0.1945em;position:relative;top:-0.0006em;\">∫</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8593em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.3442em;margin-left:-0.1945em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">a</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.2579em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">x</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3558em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">d</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> (for continuous f); integration and differentiation undo each other.</p></div><div class=\"sec eff\"><h4>✅ Why this works</h4><p>In practice the integral is estimated with a sample average (a mini-batch); it is never computed exactly.</p></div></div><div class=\"m-panel\" id=\"mt@p3\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"mt@t3\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden=\"\"><p class=\"lim\">⚠️ Limits / notes: This stop covers only what is needed; integration techniques are left out.</p></div><!--m2pi--><div class=\"sn\"><p class=\"sn-h\"><span>🔤 Symbols used here</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-all\" data-sym=\"*\">📖 All symbols</button></p><ul class=\"sn-l\"><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"frac\">▭⁄▭</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “over” (the fraction bar)</span><span class=\"sn-m\">The top is divided by the bottom. ½ is 1 divided by 2, which is one half.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"dd\">d</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “d” (a tiny change)</span><span class=\"sn-m\">“A tiny change”. d followed by something is a tiny change in it; one over another means “how fast one changes when the other changes a tiny bit” (the derivative).</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>x</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “x”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the input number</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"int\">∫</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “integral”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">The integral: cut something into countless thin strips and add them all up, e.g. the area under a curve. The small marks say where to start and stop.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>a</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “a”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">where the adding up starts</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>f</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “f”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">a function: a “machine” that takes in a number and gives back a number</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"fx\">□( )</button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “… of …”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">What comes out when you put the thing in brackets into the “machine” (function) named in front. Like a vending machine: put something in, get something out.</span></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"sn-s\" data-sym=\"var\"><i>t</i></button><span class=\"sn-r\">Say: “t”</span><span class=\"sn-m\">the positions passed while adding up (just a temporary name)</span></li></ul></div><!--/m2pi-->"}}
